# SQL's `IS NOT NULL` after a parenthesized operand, inside `and`: the fix drops the extra parentheses.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv' | where (amount + 1) IS NOT NULL and amount > 2
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..61
  PIPELINE@0..60
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 " "
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 " "
    WHERE_OP@15..60
      IDENT@15..20 "where"
      WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
      BIN_EXPR@21..60
        BIN_EXPR@21..45
          PAREN_EXPR@21..33
            L_PAREN@21..22 "("
            BIN_EXPR@22..32
              NAME_REF@22..28
                IDENT@22..28 "amount"
              WHITESPACE@28..29 " "
              PLUS@29..30 "+"
              WHITESPACE@30..31 " "
              LITERAL@31..32
                LONG@31..32 "1"
            R_PAREN@32..33 ")"
          WHITESPACE@33..34 " "
          IDENT@34..36 "IS"
          WHITESPACE@36..37 " "
          IDENT@37..40 "NOT"
          WHITESPACE@40..41 " "
          IDENT@41..45 "NULL"
        WHITESPACE@45..46 " "
        AND_KW@46..49 "and"
        WHITESPACE@49..50 " "
        BIN_EXPR@50..60
          NAME_REF@50..56
            IDENT@50..56 "amount"
          WHITESPACE@56..57 " "
          GT@57..58 ">"
          WHITESPACE@58..59 " "
          LITERAL@59..60
            LONG@59..60 "2"
  WHITESPACE@60..61 "\n"

error[DS0105]: `IS NOT NULL` is SQL, not DataScript
  --> query:1:35
  |
1 | 'orders.csv' | where (amount + 1) IS NOT NULL and amount > 2
  |                                   ^^^^^^^^^^^ this is SQL's null test
  |
  = help: test for null with `isnotnull(...)`: `isnotnull(amount + 1)`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv' | where isnotnull(amount + 1) and amount > 2
which parses without errors
